{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794674568403,"sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","part":{"id":"prt_1daf0acd3001kJpTnvnZiCYWXg","sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","messageID":"msg_1daf0a5a7001BgkzWImFJekQYS","type":"step-start","snapshot":"be6462de0e94269596f314eec33c2ccff54b1f62"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794674568496,"sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daf0acd5002ucvWKkK1E5UH6c","sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","messageID":"msg_1daf0a5a7001BgkzWImFJekQYS","type":"tool","id":"3h0fuk7tr","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind && grep -n -i \"executor kind\\|cli-mistral-vibe\\|vibe\" spec.md | head -40"},"output":"3:description: \"The deep-loop fan-out cannot run a Vibe lineage, because no executor kind, adapter, env allowlist or recursion guard names Vibe. This phase adds cli-mistral-vibe as an executor kind that runs print mode with a lineage-local VIBE_HOME and scores each lineage from export.json.\"\n5:  - \"deep loop executor kind\"\n6:  - \"phase 9 deep loop executor kind\"\n7:  - \"cli-mistral-vibe executor kind\"\n29:| **Predecessor** | 008-vibe-repo-guards |\n39:This is **Phase 9** of the Mistral Vibe runtime mode build specification.\n41:**Scope Boundary**: The `cli-mistral-vibe` executor kind in the deep-loop runtime, its fan-out adapter, its tests and the deep-loop YAML branches. No change to any other kind's behavior, to the dispatch hook library or to `.vibe/`.\n44:- 007-dispatch-recognition-and-hard-rules. The adapter's command must pass the Vibe hard rules 007 enforces. The phase plan lists 007 as this phase's only dependency.\n48:- `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts`, `executor-audit.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`.\n59:The deep-loop fan-out runs a lineage only through an executor kind with its own adapter, env allowlist and recursion guard, and none of the seven runtime, test and command files searched in Measured Behavior mentions Vibe. A research or review run cannot use Vibe as an executor, so Mistral's models are unreachable from deep loops through Vibe.\n62:A deep-loop run can name `cli-mistral-vibe` as an executor kind, and each Vibe lineage runs isolated and is scored from its `export.json`.\n68:$ rg -c 'cli-mistral-vibe|vibe' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/live-contracts.json .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml; echo \"exit=$?\"\n83:$ vibe --version\n84:vibe 3.1.2\n86:Line 26 matters because Vibe also uses exit 3, for a run stopped without finishing. Line 74 shows the binary table holds one name per kind, and Vibe needs two. The two `'partial'` lines are run-level statuses, so no per-lineage partial outcome exists yet.\n95:- Add `cli-mistral-vibe` to `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` with `model`, `timeoutSeconds` and `liveTools`, no `reasoningEffort`, and a sandbox request that fails closed. Add `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` and `isVibeSupportedModel`, holding only aliases whose model row pins `thinking`.\n96:- Add `buildVibeLineageCommand` to `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` in `fanout-run.cjs`: PATH and version preflight, roster check, a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, `--output-dir` in the lineage folder and `--trust`.\n97:- Extend `executor-audit.ts`: the `VIBE_` prefix and `MISTRAL_API_KEY` in the env allowlist, `VIBE_HOME` as lineage state, and recursion detection for `vibe-rs` and `vibe-app-server`, the names phase 004 saw in the ancestor walk (`vibe` stays harmless).\n103:- Sandbox mode - deferred because Vibe has no CLI or config field for it. The kind rejects a sandbox request rather than pretending to confine.\n104:- The session-relaunch loop - deferred because Vibe has no idle or compaction event and only an outer supervisor could drive it. A lineage is one process per iteration.\n105:- Turn-stopping guards such as completion-evidence and ask-surface - deferred because Vibe has no strict `post_agent` event, so they are not portable. Lineage scoring reads `export.json` instead.\n113:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` | Modify | Kind, flag support, sandbox, web-search and MCP rows, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` |\n114:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` | Modify | Env allowlist, `VIBE_HOME` state, two-name recursion detection |\n115:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | Modify | `buildVibeLineageCommand`, `export.json` scoring |\n117:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts` | Create | Stress fixture for the adapter |\n119:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`, `deep-review-auto.yaml` | Modify | `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branches |\n133:| REQ-001 | `cli-mistral-vibe` is an executor kind that accepts `model`, `timeoutSeconds` and `liveTools` and rejects `reasoningEffort` and any sandbox request |\n134:| REQ-002 | `isVibeSupportedModel` accepts only aliases in `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, each backed by a model row that pins `thinking` |\n135:| REQ-003 | `buildVibeLineageCommand` refuses a missing binary, a version other than 3.1.2 and an off-roster model, and builds a command with a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, `--output-dir` and `--trust` |\n136:| REQ-004 | The env allowlist passes `VIBE_`-prefixed variables and `MISTRAL_API_KEY` to a Vibe lineage, and the lineage's own `VIBE_HOME` replaces an inherited one |\n137:| REQ-005 | The recursion guard detects a Vibe ancestor under `vibe-rs` or `vibe-app-server` |\n138:| REQ-006 | A Vibe exit 3 is recorded as partial on the lineage result and never counted as success, and is told apart from the recursion guard's exit 3 |\n139:| REQ-007 | One keyed Vibe lineage runs a research iteration end to end, in the smallest fan-out the `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch accepts |\n146:| REQ-009 | The deep-research and deep-review YAMLs carry an `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch |\n158:- **SC-001**: A keyed fan-out run with one `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage beside a second executor group writes a Vibe research iteration and an `export.json` whose `exit_code` is 0.\n159:- **SC-002**: A shimmed `vibe` that writes an export with `exit_code` 3 and exits 3 leaves its lineage recorded partial and not succeeded. The kind's flag support has no budget field, so the keyed path cannot request a turn cap.\n170:| Dependency | Model aliases for `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` come from the model rows phase 006 writes, and 006 is not in this phase's dependency chain | Med | Setup reads the rows from phase 006's config. If 006 has not landed, the roster task waits and goal.md records it |\n171:| Risk | Vibe's exit 3 and `RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE` 3 collide, so a guard refusal could score as a partial run | High | A guard refusal never launches Vibe and leaves no `export.json`. Scoring reads `export.json` first, and its absence means failure |\n173:| Risk | The `VIBE_` prefix also passes an inherited `VIBE_HOME` or `VIBE_CWD` | Med | `VIBE_HOME` joins the lineage state table, as `DSH_HOME` does, and the adapter sets it last |\n182:- **NFR-P01**: The adapter preflight spawns `vibe --version` once per lineage and makes no network call.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"The deep-loop fan-out cannot run a Vibe lineage, because no executor kind, adapter, env allowlist or recursion guard names Vibe. This phase adds cli-mistral-vibe as an executor kind that runs print mode with a lineage-local VIBE_HOME and scores each lineage from export.json.\"\n5:  - \"deep loop executor kind\"\n6:  - \"phase 9 deep loop executor kind\"\n7:  - \"cli-mistral-vibe executor kind\"\n29:| **Predecessor** | 008-vibe-repo-guards |\n39:This is **Phase 9** of the Mistral Vibe runtime mode build specification.\n41:**Scope Boundary**: The `cli-mistral-vibe` executor kind in the deep-loop runtime, its fan-out adapter, its tests and the deep-loop YAML branches. No change to any other kind's behavior, to the dispatch hook library or to `.vibe/`.\n44:- 007-dispatch-recognition-and-hard-rules. The adapter's command must pass the Vibe hard rules 007 enforces. The phase plan lists 007 as this phase's only dependency.\n48:- `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts`, `executor-audit.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`.\n59:The deep-loop fan-out runs a lineage only through an executor kind with its own adapter, env allowlist and recursion guard, and none of the seven runtime, test and command files searched in Measured Behavior mentions Vibe. A research or review run cannot use Vibe as an executor, so Mistral's models are unreachable from deep loops through Vibe.\n62:A deep-loop run can name `cli-mistral-vibe` as an executor kind, and each Vibe lineage runs isolated and is scored from its `export.json`.\n68:$ rg -c 'cli-mistral-vibe|vibe' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/live-contracts.json .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml; echo \"exit=$?\"\n83:$ vibe --version\n84:vibe 3.1.2\n86:Line 26 matters because Vibe also uses exit 3, for a run stopped without finishing. Line 74 shows the binary table holds one name per kind, and Vibe needs two. The two `'partial'` lines are run-level statuses, so no per-lineage partial outcome exists yet.\n95:- Add `cli-mistral-vibe` to `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` with `model`, `timeoutSeconds` and `liveTools`, no `reasoningEffort`, and a sandbox request that fails closed. Add `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` and `isVibeSupportedModel`, holding only aliases whose model row pins `thinking`.\n96:- Add `buildVibeLineageCommand` to `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` in `fanout-run.cjs`: PATH and version preflight, roster check, a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, `--output-dir` in the lineage folder and `--trust`.\n97:- Extend `executor-audit.ts`: the `VIBE_` prefix and `MISTRAL_API_KEY` in the env allowlist, `VIBE_HOME` as lineage state, and recursion detection for `vibe-rs` and `vibe-app-server`, the names phase 004 saw in the ancestor walk (`vibe` stays harmless).\n103:- Sandbox mode - deferred because Vibe has no CLI or config field for it. The kind rejects a sandbox request rather than pretending to confine.\n104:- The session-relaunch loop - deferred because Vibe has no idle or compaction event and only an outer supervisor could drive it. A lineage is one process per iteration.\n105:- Turn-stopping guards such as completion-evidence and ask-surface - deferred because Vibe has no strict `post_agent` event, so they are not portable. Lineage scoring reads `export.json` instead.\n113:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` | Modify | Kind, flag support, sandbox, web-search and MCP rows, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` |\n114:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` | Modify | Env allowlist, `VIBE_HOME` state, two-name recursion detection |\n115:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | Modify | `buildVibeLineageCommand`, `export.json` scoring |\n117:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts` | Create | Stress fixture for the adapter |\n119:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`, `deep-review-auto.yaml` | Modify | `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branches |\n133:| REQ-001 | `cli-mistral-vibe` is an executor kind that accepts `model`, `timeoutSeconds` and `liveTools` and rejects `reasoningEffort` and any sandbox request |\n134:| REQ-002 | `isVibeSupportedModel` accepts only aliases in `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, each backed by a model row that pins `thinking` |\n135:| REQ-003 | `buildVibeLineageCommand` refuses a missing binary, a version other than 3.1.2 and an off-roster model, and builds a command with a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, `--output-dir` and `--trust` |\n136:| REQ-004 | The env allowlist passes `VIBE_`-prefixed variables and `MISTRAL_API_KEY` to a Vibe lineage, and the lineage's own `VIBE_HOME` replaces an inherited one |\n137:| REQ-005 | The recursion guard detects a Vibe ancestor under `vibe-rs` or `vibe-app-server` |\n138:| REQ-006 | A Vibe exit 3 is recorded as partial on the lineage result and never counted as success, and is told apart from the recursion guard's exit 3 |\n139:| REQ-007 | One keyed Vibe lineage runs a research iteration end to end, in the smallest fan-out the `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch accepts |\n146:| REQ-009 | The deep-research and deep-review YAMLs carry an `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch |\n158:- **SC-001**: A keyed fan-out run with one `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage beside a second executor group writes a Vibe research iteration and an `export.json` whose `exit_code` is 0.\n159:- **SC-002**: A shimmed `vibe` that writes an export with `exit_code` 3 and exits 3 leaves its lineage recorded partial and not succeeded. The kind's flag support has no budget field, so the keyed path cannot request a turn cap.\n170:| Dependency | Model aliases for `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` come from the model rows phase 006 writes, and 006 is not in this phase's dependency chain | Med | Setup reads the rows from phase 006's config. If 006 has not landed, the roster task waits and goal.md records it |\n171:| Risk | Vibe's exit 3 and `RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE` 3 collide, so a guard refusal could score as a partial run | High | A guard refusal never launches Vibe and leaves no `export.json`. Scoring reads `export.json` first, and its absence means failure |\n173:| Risk | The `VIBE_` prefix also passes an inherited `VIBE_HOME` or `VIBE_CWD` | Med | `VIBE_HOME` joins the lineage state table, as `DSH_HOME` does, and the adapter sets it last |\n182:- **NFR-P01**: The adapter preflight spawns `vibe --version` once per lineage and makes no network call.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind && grep -n -i \\\"executor kind\\\\|cli-mistral-vibe\\\\|vibe\\\" spec.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794674568405,"end":1794674568496}}}}
