{"type":"text","timestamp":1794674748720,"sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","part":{"id":"prt_1daf36d21001SF743coEirxnyw","sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","messageID":"msg_1daf366f8001CoVeR5pSdIY9jO","type":"text","text":"Now writing the iteration narrative and delta.\n\n","time":{"start":1794674748705,"end":1794674748720}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794674755983,"sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daf36d31001IWENh1wFwjzNPt","sessionID":"ses_e250f8270ffecHC0vrO03ZLgYJ","messageID":"msg_1daf366f8001CoVeR5pSdIY9jO","type":"tool","id":"7y1s90y8o","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: What the `cli-mistral-vibe` deep-loop executor kind adds\n\n## Focus\n\nThe dispatch question: in one short paragraph, what does the deep-loop executor kind\n`cli-mistral-vibe` add? The selected interpretation is the **as-built** surface in this\ncheckout (phase 009 of the Mistral Vibe runtime build), not the phase plan's forward-looking\nintent. Deferred alternative: a behavioural evaluation of the two roster models, which this\niteration does not attempt because the question asks what the *kind* adds, not how the models\nperform.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the phase packet's `spec.md` to recover the declared scope, requirements and risks.\n2. Located every non-spec file naming `cli-mistral-vibe` to establish the changed surface set.\n3. Read the executor-kind registry rows (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`, flag support, sandbox and web-search\n   rows, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `isVibeSupportedModel`, the config validator).\n4. Read the executor-audit rows (recursion names, state-dir table, default home, env prefix,\n   env keys, env deny table).\n5. Read `buildVibeLineageCommand` and the Vibe scoring helpers in `fanout-run.cjs`.\n6. Confirmed the `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch exists in both deep-loop workflow YAMLs and that\n   the stress fixture and matrix manifest register the kind.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The kind makes Mistral Vibe a first-class deep-loop executor: `cli-mistral-vibe` is a member\n   of `EXECUTOR_KINDS`, so a fan-out run can name it beside any other kind and get an\n   independent lineage instead of the \"no executor kind names Vibe\" gap the phase opened with.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:20]\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/spec.md:59]\n\n2. Its capability surface is deliberately narrow: the kind accepts only `model`, `timeoutSeconds`\n   and `liveTools`. It has no `reasoningEffort` field because Vibe has no reasoning flag — the\n   effort pin lives on the roster row — and it declares no sandbox support, so a sandbox request\n   fails closed rather than pretending to confine the process.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:141]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:168]\n\n3. Model selection is closed by an enforced two-alias allowlist, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS =\n   ['deepseek-flash', 'glm-flash']`, checked by `isVibeSupportedModel` and rejected in config\n   validation with a message naming the allowlist. A caller cannot route a Vibe lineage to an\n   arbitrary Mistral model.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:301]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:705]\n\n4. The adapter `buildVibeLineageCommand` gives each lineage its own runtime state: it preflights\n   the binary, probes `vibe --version` in a throwaway home, refuses any version other than\n   `3.1.2`, refuses an off-roster model, then writes a lineage-local `vibe-home` seeded from\n   `.vibe/config.toml` plus a `trusted_folders.toml` naming the resolved lineage directory, and\n   runs `vibe --prompt-file … --output-dir <lineage>/vibe-output --trust --model … --auto-approve`\n   with cwd set to the lineage.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3154]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3200]\n\n5. The audit layer admits Vibe without leaking operator state: `VIBE_`-prefixed variables and\n   `MISTRAL_API_KEY` pass through, while an inherited `VIBE_HOME` is explicitly denied so the\n   runner's per-lineage home wins, and `VIBE_HOME` is registered as lineage state with `.vibe` as\n   the default home directory. Recursion is detected on `vibe`, `vibe-rs` and `vibe-app-server`.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:77]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:174]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:199]\n\n6. Vibe lineages are scored from the run's own export record rather than from stdout or exit\n   status alone: `resolveVibeLineageOutcome` returns `success` only when the process exits 0,\n   `export.json` exists, its `exit_code` is 0 and its `outcome` is absent or `finished`; exit 3\n   with an export record is `partial`; everything else is `failure`. That is what separates a\n   stopped-but-recorded Vibe run from a genuine success.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3126]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3137]\n\n7. The kind is wired into the loop surface, not just the runtime: `buildVibeLineageCommand` is\n   registered in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS`, and both `deep-research-auto.yaml` and\n   `deep-review-auto.yaml` carry an `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch that fails closed with exit 2\n   when a single-executor run names Vibe, directing the caller to a fan-out invocation.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3256]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml:1223]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:1252]\n\n8. The kind ships with its own conformance coverage: a stress fixture asserts the shipped argv\n   shape, clean-exit success, exit-3 partial, and fail-closed exit 3 without an export record, and\n   the adapter matrix manifest registers `cli-mistral-vibe` so the kind cannot silently drop out\n   of the cross-kind matrix.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts:154]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:13]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- What does the deep-loop executor kind cli-mistral-vibe add?\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Which runtime surfaces change when the kind is added — answered in substance by findings 1-8,\n  but not ticked in this iteration because the run's iteration budget is one and the strategy\n  question was scoped to the kind's contribution.\n- What isolation and scoring guarantees does a Vibe lineage get that no existing executor kind\n  provides — partially answered (lineage-local home, export-record scoring, two-name recursion\n  guard); a cross-kind comparison against `cli-deepseek-harness` remains open.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reading the phase plan (`plan.md`) as the answer source: it states intended design, and the\n  question asks what the kind *adds* in the code that exists. The plan was used only as\n  cross-check, and the as-built code was preferred wherever the two could differ.\n- Evaluating model quality of `deepseek-flash` / `glm-flash`: out of scope for a question about\n  the kind's contribution.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- None. Every targeted surface existed and answered the question.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: the question admits a plan-intent reading and an as-built reading. Selected\n  as-built; plan-intent deferred.\n- Contradictory evidence: none found. The spec's REQ rows and the code agree on the flag set,\n  the allowlist and the exit-3 handling.\n- Missing dependencies: none. The `.vibe/config.toml` seed that the adapter requires exists in\n  the checkout, so the adapter's precondition is satisfiable.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/spec.md\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\n- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\n- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/steer.md (absent; no lead ruling to apply)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.90\n- Questions addressed: 3\n- Questions answered: 1\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: starting from the phase spec and then walking the exact files the spec's\n  measured-behaviour row names meant every code read landed on a surface the phase actually\n  changed, so eight findings came out of six targeted reads with no dead ends.\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed. The only friction was that the lineage directory\n  holds no config or strategy at start — phase_init had to author them before the gateway would\n  accept a run-opening row, which is expected for a detached lineage.\n- What I would do differently: with a second iteration, I would compare this kind field-by-field\n  against `cli-deepseek-harness`, the closest existing kind, to isolate what is genuinely new\n  about Vibe rather than what follows the shared adapter pattern.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nCross-kind comparison: diff the `cli-mistral-vibe` rows against `cli-deepseek-harness` in\n`executor-config.ts` and `executor-audit.ts` to separate Vibe-specific guarantees (export-record\nscoring, two-name recursion guard, version pin) from the shared fan-out adapter boilerplate.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 1: What the `cli-mistral-vibe` deep-loop executor kind adds\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nThe dispatch question: in one short paragraph, what does the deep-loop executor kind\\n`cli-mistral-vibe` add? The selected interpretation is the **as-built** surface in this\\ncheckout (phase 009 of the Mistral Vibe runtime build), not the phase plan's forward-looking\\nintent. Deferred alternative: a behavioural evaluation of the two roster models, which this\\niteration does not attempt because the question asks what the *kind* adds, not how the models\\nperform.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the phase packet's `spec.md` to recover the declared scope, requirements and risks.\\n2. Located every non-spec file naming `cli-mistral-vibe` to establish the changed surface set.\\n3. Read the executor-kind registry rows (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`, flag support, sandbox and web-search\\n   rows, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `isVibeSupportedModel`, the config validator).\\n4. Read the executor-audit rows (recursion names, state-dir table, default home, env prefix,\\n   env keys, env deny table).\\n5. Read `buildVibeLineageCommand` and the Vibe scoring helpers in `fanout-run.cjs`.\\n6. Confirmed the `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch exists in both deep-loop workflow YAMLs and that\\n   the stress fixture and matrix manifest register the kind.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The kind makes Mistral Vibe a first-class deep-loop executor: `cli-mistral-vibe` is a member\\n   of `EXECUTOR_KINDS`, so a fan-out run can name it beside any other kind and get an\\n   independent lineage instead of the \\\"no executor kind names Vibe\\\" gap the phase opened with.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:20]\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/spec.md:59]\\n\\n2. Its capability surface is deliberately narrow: the kind accepts only `model`, `timeoutSeconds`\\n   and `liveTools`. It has no `reasoningEffort` field because Vibe has no reasoning flag — the\\n   effort pin lives on the roster row — and it declares no sandbox support, so a sandbox request\\n   fails closed rather than pretending to confine the process.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:141]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:168]\\n\\n3. Model selection is closed by an enforced two-alias allowlist, `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS =\\n   ['deepseek-flash', 'glm-flash']`, checked by `isVibeSupportedModel` and rejected in config\\n   validation with a message naming the allowlist. A caller cannot route a Vibe lineage to an\\n   arbitrary Mistral model.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:301]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:705]\\n\\n4. The adapter `buildVibeLineageCommand` gives each lineage its own runtime state: it preflights\\n   the binary, probes `vibe --version` in a throwaway home, refuses any version other than\\n   `3.1.2`, refuses an off-roster model, then writes a lineage-local `vibe-home` seeded from\\n   `.vibe/config.toml` plus a `trusted_folders.toml` naming the resolved lineage directory, and\\n   runs `vibe --prompt-file … --output-dir <lineage>/vibe-output --trust --model … --auto-approve`\\n   with cwd set to the lineage.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3154]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3200]\\n\\n5. The audit layer admits Vibe without leaking operator state: `VIBE_`-prefixed variables and\\n   `MISTRAL_API_KEY` pass through, while an inherited `VIBE_HOME` is explicitly denied so the\\n   runner's per-lineage home wins, and `VIBE_HOME` is registered as lineage state with `.vibe` as\\n   the default home directory. Recursion is detected on `vibe`, `vibe-rs` and `vibe-app-server`.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:77]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:174]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:199]\\n\\n6. Vibe lineages are scored from the run's own export record rather than from stdout or exit\\n   status alone: `resolveVibeLineageOutcome` returns `success` only when the process exits 0,\\n   `export.json` exists, its `exit_code` is 0 and its `outcome` is absent or `finished`; exit 3\\n   with an export record is `partial`; everything else is `failure`. That is what separates a\\n   stopped-but-recorded Vibe run from a genuine success.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3126]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3137]\\n\\n7. The kind is wired into the loop surface, not just the runtime: `buildVibeLineageCommand` is\\n   registered in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS`, and both `deep-research-auto.yaml` and\\n   `deep-review-auto.yaml` carry an `if_cli_mistral_vibe` branch that fails closed with exit 2\\n   when a single-executor run names Vibe, directing the caller to a fan-out invocation.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3256]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml:1223]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:1252]\\n\\n8. The kind ships with its own conformance coverage: a stress fixture asserts the shipped argv\\n   shape, clean-exit success, exit-3 partial, and fail-closed exit 3 without an export record, and\\n   the adapter matrix manifest registers `cli-mistral-vibe` so the kind cannot silently drop out\\n   of the cross-kind matrix.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts:154]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:13]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- What does the deep-loop executor kind cli-mistral-vibe add?\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Which runtime surfaces change when the kind is added — answered in substance by findings 1-8,\\n  but not ticked in this iteration because the run's iteration budget is one and the strategy\\n  question was scoped to the kind's contribution.\\n- What isolation and scoring guarantees does a Vibe lineage get that no existing executor kind\\n  provides — partially answered (lineage-local home, export-record scoring, two-name recursion\\n  guard); a cross-kind comparison against `cli-deepseek-harness` remains open.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Reading the phase plan (`plan.md`) as the answer source: it states intended design, and the\\n  question asks what the kind *adds* in the code that exists. The plan was used only as\\n  cross-check, and the as-built code was preferred wherever the two could differ.\\n- Evaluating model quality of `deepseek-flash` / `glm-flash`: out of scope for a question about\\n  the kind's contribution.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- None. Every targeted surface existed and answered the question.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: the question admits a plan-intent reading and an as-built reading. Selected\\n  as-built; plan-intent deferred.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none found. The spec's REQ rows and the code agree on the flag set,\\n  the allowlist and the exit-3 handling.\\n- Missing dependencies: none. The `.vibe/config.toml` seed that the adapter requires exists in\\n  the checkout, so the adapter's precondition is satisfiable.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/spec.md\\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts\\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts\\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\\n- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\\n- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-mistral-vibe.vitest.ts\\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts\\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/steer.md (absent; no lead ruling to apply)\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.90\\n- Questions addressed: 3\\n- Questions answered: 1\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: starting from the phase spec and then walking the exact files the spec's\\n  measured-behaviour row names meant every code read landed on a surface the phase actually\\n  changed, so eight findings came out of six targeted reads with no dead ends.\\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed. The only friction was that the lineage directory\\n  holds no config or strategy at start — phase_init had to author them before the gateway would\\n  accept a run-opening row, which is expected for a detached lineage.\\n- What I would do differently: with a second iteration, I would compare this kind field-by-field\\n  against `cli-deepseek-harness`, the closest existing kind, to isolate what is genuinely new\\n  about Vibe rather than what follows the shared adapter pattern.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nCross-kind comparison: diff the `cli-mistral-vibe` rows against `cli-deepseek-harness` in\\n`executor-config.ts` and `executor-audit.ts` to separate Vibe-specific guarantees (export-record\\nscoring, two-name recursion guard, version pin) from the shared fan-out adapter boilerplate.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/009-deep-loop-executor-kind/research/keyed-lineage-run/lineages/oc-1/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794674748721,"end":1794674755983}}}}
